  "script_text": "This is the Food Line briefing for June 5, 2026.\n\n13abc reported that Toledo food pantries were preparing for increased demand as SNAP benefits faced a shutdown pause.\n\nWhen benefits are delayed or paused, food pantries may see higher demand from households that rely on SNAP.\n\nIn Toledo, 13abc reported rising food-assistance demand affecting SNAP households.\n\nWe are also watching two related food-access reports.\n\nCascade PBS reported that Washington food banks were worried about federal food-program cuts.\n\nKLTV reported that East Texas food banks were working to keep up with rising demand during the government shutdown.\n\nSource links, excerpts, and background references are available in the public source table.\n\nThis has been the Food Line briefing from The Blue Fern Co.",
